This is the "MIT OR Apache-2.0" dual license SPDX expression used by every
crate in the `figtether` workspace (`license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"` in
`Cargo.toml`). You may choose either license, and you may not use the
work under both licenses at the same time.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

Why dual licensing
------------------

MIT is the shortest permissive license that most contributors already know,
and it keeps embedding FigTether in other tools simple. Apache-2.0 adds an
express patent grant and defined contribution terms, which matters for a tool
that touches third-party editor APIs. Offering both lets a downstream user
pick the terms that fit their own distribution model. The rationale is
recorded in `docs/02-architecture/adr/ADR-009-licensing.md`.

Third-party material
--------------------

Third-party dependencies keep their own licenses. Their attributions are
collected in `NOTICE`, and the exact inventory for a release is shipped in the
CycloneDX SBOM. Nothing in this file changes or narrows the license of any
dependency.

Full texts
